  "description": "Borrowing from the Mexican pantry, this easy, warming soup is made with roasted butternut squash, flavored with ancho chiles, and garnished with Mexican crema, cilantro, and pepitas.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Mexican crema or sour cream, for garnish; Cilantro leaves, for garnish; Pepitas (toasted pumpkin seeds), for garnish; Lime wedges, for serving\n\nOptional substitutions: chicken stock → low-sodium broth\n\nNotes: If you want a less spicy soup with a less intense chile flavor, feel free to discard the ancho chile seeds or scale down to one ancho chile pepper. Otherwise, go for the big flavor and spoon in plenty of crema or sour cream to tame the intensity. You can make this soup vegetarian by substituting with vegetable stock.",
  "author": [
    "Daniel Gritzer"
  ],
